  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 1626.04 Warning Signal",
  "priorExpiration": "2005-01-10",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 1626.04 Warning Signal.\n\n(a) Before a blast is fired, a loud warning signal shall be given by the person in charge, who has made certain that:\n\n(1) All surplus explosives are in a safe place;\n\n(2) All persons and vehicles are at a safe distance or under sufficient cover; and\n\n(3) An adequate warning has been given.\n\n(b) For the purposes of this section, a loud warning signal means that it is capable of being heard by people within the landing area of the blasting site in which debris might fall.\n\nSource. #2220, eff 12-31-82; ss by #2837, eff 8-27-84; ss by #4584, eff 3-3-89; ss by #5996, INTERIM, eff 3-3-95, EXPIRES, 7-1-95; ss by #6054, eff 7-1-95, EXPIRED: 7-1-03\n\nNew. #8116, INTERIM, eff 7-14-04, EXPIRES: 1-10-05; ss by #8231, eff 12-20-04; ss by #10396, eff 8-15-13",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c1600.html"
